INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('156','16','1','What is the main purpose of an analytical exposition text','1','To entertain the audience with stories.','To describe a process in detail.','To persuade the readers or listeners about a particular viewpoint.','To provide a summary of events.','To inform readers about factual information.','C',NULL,'','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('157','16','2','What is one characteristic that distinguishes analytical exposition from other types of texts?','1','It uses a narrative style to tell a story.','It focuses on providing logical arguments and reasoning.','It is primarily descriptive in nature.',' It includes fictional elements to engage readers.','It is written in a poetic format.','B',NULL,'','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('158','16','3','<p>I strongly believe that mobile phones are necessary. My reasons for this belief are that these phones are convenient for business people who travel a lot, and they are handy for emergencies.</p>\r\n<p>To begin with, mobile phones are necessary in the case of emergencies. For instance, if you fall down a set of stairs in a building and are badly injured and can&rsquo;t reach a pay phone, it is handy to have one to use. Or, if your car breaks down in the middle of the night in a strange neighbourhood, it would be dangerous to leave it in search of a public phone booth.</p>\r\n<p>My other main reason is that mobile phones are convenient for business people. For example, if you are out of the state or even overseas and you have to contact a client to do some important work, it is useful to have one to use. By using a mobile phone, important information can be received. People can&rsquo;t stay in an office all day waiting for their phone to ring. Some people have to go and do jobs or they will go out of business. You can even send faxes or messages and use the internet with your mobile.</p>\r\n<p>In conclusion, I believe that mobile phones have now become a necessary part of every day life. Instant communication will ensure that information can be passed on with a simple press of a button. Whether this is to do with business or personal information or emergencies, it goes to show that they are necessary in the new millennium.</p>\r\n<p>How many reasons are used to support the writer&rsquo;s opinion?</p>','1','<p>One reason</p>','<p>Two reasons</p>','<p>Three reasons</p>','<p>Four reasons</p>','<p>Five reasons</p>','B','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('159','16','4','<p>I strongly believe that mobile phones are necessary. My reasons for this belief are that these phones are convenient for business people who travel a lot, and they are handy for emergencies.</p>\r\n<p>To begin with, mobile phones are necessary in the case of emergencies. For instance, if you fall down a set of stairs in a building and are badly injured and can&rsquo;t reach a pay phone, it is handy to have one to use. Or, if your car breaks down in the middle of the night in a strange neighbourhood, it would be dangerous to leave it in search of a public phone booth.</p>\r\n<p>My other main reason is that mobile phones are convenient for business people. For example, if you are out of the state or even overseas and you have to contact a client to do some important work, it is useful to have one to use. By using a mobile phone, important information can be received. People can&rsquo;t stay in an office all day waiting for their phone to ring. Some people have to go and do jobs or they will go out of business. You can even send faxes or messages and use the internet with your mobile.</p>\r\n<p>In conclusion, I believe that mobile phones have now become a necessary part of every day life. Instant communication will ensure that information can be passed on with a simple press of a button. Whether this is to do with business or personal information or emergencies, it goes to show that they are necessary in the new millennium.</p>\r\n<p>Why are mobile phones very convenient for bussines people?</p>','1','<p>They can contact clients</p>','<p>They can do some important works</p>','<p>They can receive some important information</p>','<p>They can send some data and surf Internet</p>','<p>They can run bussines by staying in and out office.</p>','E','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('160','16','5','<p>I strongly believe that mobile phones are necessary. My reasons for this belief are that these phones are convenient for business people who travel a lot, and they are handy for emergencies.</p>\r\n<p>To begin with, mobile phones are necessary in the case of emergencies. For instance, if you fall down a set of stairs in a building and are badly injured and can&rsquo;t reach a pay phone, it is handy to have one to use. Or, if your car breaks down in the middle of the night in a strange neighbourhood, it would be dangerous to leave it in search of a public phone booth.</p>\r\n<p>My other main reason is that mobile phones are convenient for business people. For example, if you are out of the state or even overseas and you have to contact a client to do some important work, it is useful to have one to use. By using a mobile phone, important information can be received. People can&rsquo;t stay in an office all day waiting for their phone to ring. Some people have to go and do jobs or they will go out of business. You can even send faxes or messages and use the internet with your mobile.</p>\r\n<p>In conclusion, I believe that mobile phones have now become a necessary part of every day life. Instant communication will ensure that information can be passed on with a simple press of a button. Whether this is to do with business or personal information or emergencies, it goes to show that they are necessary in the new millennium.</p>\r\n<p>What is the main idea of the second paragraph?</p>','1','<p>The advantages cellular phones during the emergencies</p>','<p>The solution to do when your car breaks down</p>','<p>The danger to leave a mobile phone in the car</p>','<p>The differences of a mobile phone and a pay phone</p>','<p>The necessary equipments among neighbours</p>','A','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('161','16','6','<p>Learning English through music and songs can be very enjoyable. You can mix pleasure with learning when you listen to a song and exploit the song as a means to your English progress. Some underlying reason can be drawn to support the idea why we use songs in language learning.<br />Firstly, &ldquo;the song stuck in my head&rdquo; Phenomenon (the echoing in our minds of the last song we heard after leaving a restaurant, shopping malls, etc) can be both enjoyable and sometimes unnerving. This phenomenon also seems to reinforce the idea that songs work on our short-and-long term memory.<br />Secondly, songs in general also use simple conversational language, with a lot of repetition, which is just what many learners look for sample text. The fact that they are effective makes them many times more motivating than other text. Although usually simple, some songs can be quite complex syntactically, lexically and poetically, and can be analyzed in the same way as any other literary sample.<br />Furthermore, song can be appropriated by listener for their own purpose. Most pop songs and probably many other types don&rsquo;t have precise people, place or time reference.<br />In addition, songs are relaxing. They provide variety and fun, and encourage harmony within oneself and within one group. Little wonder they are important tools in sustaining culture, religion, patriotism and yeas, even revolution.<br />Last but not least, there are many learning activities we can do with songs such as studying grammar, practicing selective listening comprehension, translating songs, learning vocabulary, spelling and culture.<br />From the elaboration above, it can be concluded that learning through music and songs, learning English can be enjoyable and fun.</p>\r\n<p>What is the communicative purpose of the text?</p>','1','<p>To tell the reader about the songs</p>','<p>To entertain the reader with the songs</p>','<p>To show the reader the use of songs</p>','<p>To explain above the songs</p>','<p>To persuade the reader to use songs in learning language</p>','E','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('162','16','7','<p>Learning English through music and songs can be very enjoyable. You can mix pleasure with learning when you listen to a song and exploit the song as a means to your English progress. Some underlying reason can be drawn to support the idea why we use songs in language learning.<br />Firstly, &ldquo;the song stuck in my head&rdquo; Phenomenon (the echoing in our minds of the last song we heard after leaving a restaurant, shopping malls, etc) can be both enjoyable and sometimes unnerving. This phenomenon also seems to reinforce the idea that songs work on our short-and-long term memory.<br />Secondly, songs in general also use simple conversational language, with a lot of repetition, which is just what many learners look for sample text. The fact that they are effective makes them many times more motivating than other text. Although usually simple, some songs can be quite complex syntactically, lexically and poetically, and can be analyzed in the same way as any other literary sample.<br />Furthermore, song can be appropriated by listener for their own purpose. Most pop songs and probably many other types don&rsquo;t have precise people, place or time reference.<br />In addition, songs are relaxing. They provide variety and fun, and encourage harmony within oneself and within one group. Little wonder they are important tools in sustaining culture, religion, patriotism and yeas, even revolution.<br />Last but not least, there are many learning activities we can do with songs such as studying grammar, practicing selective listening comprehension, translating songs, learning vocabulary, spelling and culture.<br />From the elaboration above, it can be concluded that learning through music and songs, learning English can be enjoyable and fun.</p>\r\n<p>What is the text about &hellip;.</p>','1','<p>Learning songs</p>','<p>Very enjoyable music</p>','<p>The phenomenon</p>','<p>Music listeners</p>','<p>Using songs in language learning</p>','E','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('163','16','8','<p>Learning English through music and songs can be very enjoyable. You can mix pleasure with learning when you listen to a song and exploit the song as a means to your English progress. Some underlying reason can be drawn to support the idea why we use songs in language learning.<br />Firstly, &ldquo;the song stuck in my head&rdquo; Phenomenon (the echoing in our minds of the last song we heard after leaving a restaurant, shopping malls, etc) can be both enjoyable and sometimes unnerving. This phenomenon also seems to reinforce the idea that songs work on our short-and-long term memory.<br />Secondly, songs in general also use simple conversational language, with a lot of repetition, which is just what many learners look for sample text. The fact that they are effective makes them many times more motivating than other text. Although usually simple, some songs can be quite complex syntactically, lexically and poetically, and can be analyzed in the same way as any other literary sample.<br />Furthermore, song can be appropriated by listener for their own purpose. Most pop songs and probably many other types don&rsquo;t have precise people, place or time reference.<br />In addition, songs are relaxing. They provide variety and fun, and encourage harmony within oneself and within one group. Little wonder they are important tools in sustaining culture, religion, patriotism and yeas, even revolution.<br />Last but not least, there are many learning activities we can do with songs such as studying grammar, practicing selective listening comprehension, translating songs, learning vocabulary, spelling and culture.<br />From the elaboration above, it can be concluded that learning through music and songs, learning English can be enjoyable and fun.</p>\r\n<p>Based on the text, there are &hellip;&hellip; reason for using songs in learning language</p>','1','<p>6</p>','<p>4</p>','<p>5</p>','<p>3</p>','<p>2</p>','B','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('164','16','9','<p>Learning English through music and songs can be very enjoyable. You can mix pleasure with learning when you listen to a song and exploit the song as a means to your English progress. Some underlying reason can be drawn to support the idea why we use songs in language learning.<br />Firstly, &ldquo;the song stuck in my head&rdquo; Phenomenon (the echoing in our minds of the last song we heard after leaving a restaurant, shopping malls, etc) can be both enjoyable and sometimes unnerving. This phenomenon also seems to reinforce the idea that songs work on our short-and-long term memory.<br />Secondly, songs in general also use simple conversational language, with a lot of repetition, which is just what many learners look for sample text. The fact that they are effective makes them many times more motivating than other text. Although usually simple, some songs can be quite complex syntactically, lexically and poetically, and can be analyzed in the same way as any other literary sample.<br />Furthermore, song can be appropriated by listener for their own purpose. Most pop songs and probably many other types don&rsquo;t have precise people, place or time reference.<br />In addition, songs are relaxing. They provide variety and fun, and encourage harmony within oneself and within one group. Little wonder they are important tools in sustaining culture, religion, patriotism and yeas, even revolution.<br />Last but not least, there are many learning activities we can do with songs such as studying grammar, practicing selective listening comprehension, translating songs, learning vocabulary, spelling and culture.<br />From the elaboration above, it can be concluded that learning through music and songs, learning English can be enjoyable and fun.</p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;They provide variety and fun, and encourage harmony within oneself and within one group.&rdquo; The<strong>&nbsp;they</strong>&nbsp;word refers to &hellip;&hellip;.</p>','1','<p>Groups</p>','<p>Learners</p>','<p>People</p>','<p>Songs</p>','<p>Activities</p>','D','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('165','16','11','<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Guide to Using a Computer for a beginner&rsquo;s</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Power On: Locate the power button on your computer\'s case or monitor. Press it to turn on the computer.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Using the Mouse:</strong> Left-click to select items, right-click to open a context menu, and drag and drop to move items.</li>\r\n<li>Login: If prompted, enter your username and password to access your user account.</li>\r\n<li>Desktop: The desktop is the main screen where you interact with your computer.</li>\r\n<li>Icons: These are shortcuts to applications, files, and folders. Double-click an icon to open the corresponding item.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>How do you select a specific item on the computer screen?</p>','1','<p>Press the spacebar.</p>','<p>Right-click on the item</p>','<p>Left-click on the item</p>','<p>Double-click the item</p>','<p>Drag and drop the item</p>','C','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('166','16','12','<p>If you have a debit card for your account, you can use that to get cash out of an Automatic Teller Machine. Insert your card through the machine. The machine will ask a for your PIN Number. The machine will verify and will ask you a series of questions of what you would like to do. Select withdrawal, then select or type in the amount you want to take out, and wait for you receipt to be printed. Remove your card from the slot. The drawer will open with a receipt and your cash withdrawal. Most machines will let you take up to five hundred dollars.</p>\r\n<p>What is the text about?</p>','1','<p>How to take money from ATM.&nbsp;</p>','<p>How to make an account at an ATM</p>','<p>How to make a loan at an ATM</p>','<p>How to use an ATM</p>','<p>How to remove the card from the slot</p>','D','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('167','16','13','<p>School uniform is special clothes worn by all students of a particular school. The uniform of a school may differ from others. Why should schools use uniforms? Below are some reasons.<br />First of all, Notre Dame&rsquo;s Department of Sociology produced a study in 1998 concerning school uniforms. Their findings using 10th grade students showed that uniforms have no direct effect on &ldquo;substance abuse, behavioral problems or attendance.&rdquo; It also claimed a negative effect on student achievements for those students considered &lsquo;pro-school&rsquo;.<br />Secondly, uniform helps to create a strong sense school ethos and a sense of belonging to a particular community. As such it promotes discipline and helps to drive up academic standards, which is why a uniform is often adopted by schools which are being reopened with a fresh start after being classified as failing.<br />Finally, uniform acts as a social leveler, under which all students are equal in the eyes of the school and of each other. In institutions without uniform students are often competitive and worry endlessly about their appearance and the clothes they should wear. Pupils without expensive designer clothes and trainers may be singled out as social outcasts, or stigmatized as being from poor backgrounds. For these reasons many parents prefer uniforms as they save them money on buying clothes for school wear. Considering the findings, schools should implement the uniform as their identity. The government should also publish some kind of rule which makes uniform compulsory for schools.</p>\r\n<p>What is the text about?</p>','1','<p>The school rules</p>','<p>The school identity</p>','<p>What we should wear at school</p>','<p>The importance of school uniform</p>','<p>The equally among students</p>','D','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('168','16','14','<p>School uniform is special clothes worn by all students of a particular school. The uniform of a school may differ from others. Why should schools use uniforms? Below are some reasons.<br />First of all, Notre Dame&rsquo;s Department of Sociology produced a study in 1998 concerning school uniforms. Their findings using 10th grade students showed that uniforms have no direct effect on &ldquo;substance abuse, behavioral problems or attendance.&rdquo; It also claimed a negative effect on student achievements for those students considered &lsquo;pro-school&rsquo;.<br />Secondly, uniform helps to create a strong sense school ethos and a sense of belonging to a particular community. As such it promotes discipline and helps to drive up academic standards, which is why a uniform is often adopted by schools which are being reopened with a fresh start after being classified as failing.<br />Finally, uniform acts as a social leveler, under which all students are equal in the eyes of the school and of each other. In institutions without uniform students are often competitive and worry endlessly about their appearance and the clothes they should wear. Pupils without expensive designer clothes and trainers may be singled out as social outcasts, or stigmatized as being from poor backgrounds. For these reasons many parents prefer uniforms as they save them money on buying clothes for school wear. Considering the findings, schools should implement the uniform as their identity. The government should also publish some kind of rule which makes uniform compulsory for schools.</p>\r\n<p>In institutions without uniform students, one will be regarded poor because he/she &hellip;.</p>','1','<p>Does not wear a school uniform</p>','<p>Cannot afford to buy a school uniform</p>','<p>Wears no expensive designer clothes</p>','<p>Posses a bad academic record</p>','<p>Has a bad attitude at school</p>','C','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('169','16','15','<p>School uniform is special clothes worn by all students of a particular school. The uniform of a school may differ from others. Why should schools use uniforms? Below are some reasons.<br />First of all, Notre Dame&rsquo;s Department of Sociology produced a study in 1998 concerning school uniforms. Their findings using 10th grade students showed that uniforms have no direct effect on &ldquo;substance abuse, behavioral problems or attendance.&rdquo; It also claimed a negative effect on student achievements for those students considered &lsquo;pro-school&rsquo;.<br />Secondly, uniform helps to create a strong sense school ethos and a sense of belonging to a particular community. As such it promotes discipline and helps to drive up academic standards, which is why a uniform is often adopted by schools which are being reopened with a fresh start after being classified as failing.<br />Finally, uniform acts as a social leveler, under which all students are equal in the eyes of the school and of each other. In institutions without uniform students are often competitive and worry endlessly about their appearance and the clothes they should wear. Pupils without expensive designer clothes and trainers may be singled out as social outcasts, or stigmatized as being from poor backgrounds. For these reasons many parents prefer uniforms as they save them money on buying clothes for school wear. Considering the findings, schools should implement the uniform as their identity. The government should also publish some kind of rule which makes uniform compulsory for schools.</p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;As such<strong>&nbsp;it</strong>&nbsp;promotes discipline and helps to drive up academic standards &hellip;&hellip;&rdquo; (Paragraph 3). What does the&nbsp;<strong>it</strong>&nbsp;word refer?</p>','1','<p>Community</p>','<p>School ethos</p>','<p>Research finding</p>','<p>A study</p>','<p>Uniform</p>','E','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('170','16','16','<p>School uniform is special clothes worn by all students of a particular school. The uniform of a school may differ from others. Why should schools use uniforms? Below are some reasons.<br />First of all, Notre Dame&rsquo;s Department of Sociology produced a study in 1998 concerning school uniforms. Their findings using 10th grade students showed that uniforms have no direct effect on &ldquo;substance abuse, behavioral problems or <strong>attendance</strong>.&rdquo; It also claimed a negative effect on student achievements for those students considered &lsquo;pro-school&rsquo;.<br />Secondly, uniform helps to create a strong sense school ethos and a sense of belonging to a particular community. As such it promotes discipline and helps to drive up academic standards, which is why a uniform is often adopted by schools which are being reopened with a fresh start after being classified as failing.<br />Finally, uniform acts as a social leveler, under which all students are equal in the eyes of the school and of each other. In institutions without uniform students are often competitive and worry endlessly about their appearance and the clothes they should wear. Pupils without expensive designer clothes and trainers may be singled out as social outcasts, or stigmatized as being from poor backgrounds. For these reasons many parents prefer uniforms as they save them money on buying clothes for school wear. Considering the findings, schools should implement the uniform as their identity. The government should also publish some kind of rule which makes uniform compulsory for schools.</p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;&hellip;. Substance abuse, behavioral problems or attendance.&rdquo; (Paragraph 2). The synonym of &ldquo;<strong>attendance</strong>&rdquo; word is &hellip;&hellip;.</p>','1','<p>Avoidance</p>','<p>Neglect</p>','<p>Nonattendance</p>','<p>Presence</p>','<p>Absence</p>','D','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('171','16','17','Which of the following is NOT a typical feature of an analytical exposition text?','1','Thesis statement',' Arguments ',' Use of first person pronouns (I, me)',' Supporting facts and data ','Reiteration','C',NULL,'','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('172','16','18','Which of the following is an example of a thesis statement for an analytical exposition text?','1','I like to eat pizza. ','Fast food is unhealthy and should be avoided','Many people enjoy watching movies','How to make a sandwich.','The weather today is sunny.','B',NULL,'','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('173','16','19','<p>Smoking in restaurants is just not disturbing. It must not be allowed because it is rude, harmful to others and dangerous for the smokers.<br />Firstly, smoking in a restaurant is impolite. The smell of the smoke affects all people and can turn them off their food. People pay to taste good food and not to be put off by foul smelling smoke.<br />Another reason smoking should not be allowed in restaurant is the harm it can do to others. Passive smoking that is breathing in smoke made by a smoker can lead to asthma attacks and even cancer.<br />Finally, smoking is dangerous and a health risk to the smokers. Cigarettes cause heart and lung disease and people should not smoke anywhere, not just in restaurants.<br />Therefore, smoking in restaurants is impolite, harmful to others and a health risk to the smokers and should not be allowed in any restaurants</p>\r\n<p>We have many reasons to say that smoking must be avoided. The word <strong>reasons</strong> mean&hellip;..</p>','1','<p>Argument</p>','<p>Point Of View</p>','<p>Conclution</p>','<p>Reinforcement</p>','<p>Statement</p>','A','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('174','16','20','<p>Smoking in restaurants is just not disturbing. It must not be allowed because it is rude, harmful to others and dangerous for the smokers.<br />Firstly, smoking in a restaurant is impolite. The smell of the smoke affects all people and can turn them off their food. People pay to taste good food and not to be put off by foul smelling smoke.<br />Another reason smoking should not be allowed in restaurant is the harm it can do to others. Passive smoking that is breathing in smoke made by a smoker can lead to asthma attacks and even cancer.<br />Finally, smoking is dangerous and a health risk to the smokers. Cigarettes cause heart and lung disease and people should not smoke anywhere, not just in restaurants.<br />Therefore, smoking in restaurants is impolite, harmful to others and a health risk to the smokers and should not be allowed in any restaurants</p>\r\n<p>.The synonym of the word <strong>dangerous</strong> in the text is&hellip;</p>','1','<p>Rude</p>','<p>Impolite</p>','<p>Health risk</p>','<p>Harmful</p>','<p>Disease</p>','C','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('175','16','21','<p>How to make a Cheese Omelet</p>\r\n<p>Ingredients:</p>\r\n<p>1 egg, 50 g cheese,1 cup milk, 3 tablespoons cooking oil, a pinch of salt and pepper.</p>\r\n<p>Utensils:</p>\r\n<p>Frying pan, fork, spatula, cheese-grater, bowl, and plate.</p>\r\n<p>Method:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Crack the egg into a bowl</li>\r\n<li>Whisk the egg with a fork until it&rsquo;s smooth</li>\r\n<li>Add milk and whisk well</li>\r\n<li>Grate the cheese into the bowl and stir</li>\r\n<li>Heat the oil in frying pan</li>\r\n<li>Turn the omelet with spatula and cook both sides</li>\r\n<li>Place on a plate, season with salt and pepper</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The text tells us about&hellip;</p>','1','<p>How long to make any kind of food</p>','<p>Ingredients of making omelet</p>','<p>Utensils of making omelet</p>','<p>Methods of making omelet</p>','<p>How to eat a cheese omelet</p>','D','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('176','16','22','<p>How to make a Cheese Omelet</p>\r\n<p>Ingredients:</p>\r\n<p>1 egg, 50 g cheese,1 cup milk, 3 tablespoons cooking oil, a pinch of salt and pepper.</p>\r\n<p>Utensils:</p>\r\n<p>Frying pan, fork, spatula, cheese-grater, bowl, and plate.</p>\r\n<p>Method:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Crack the egg into a bowl</li>\r\n<li>Whisk the egg with a fork until it&rsquo;s smooth</li>\r\n<li>Add milk and whisk well</li>\r\n<li>Grate the cheese into the bowl and stir</li>\r\n<li>Heat the oil in frying pan</li>\r\n<li>Turn the omelet with spatula and cook both sides</li>\r\n<li>Place on a plate, season with salt and pepper</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&hellip;..lemonade extract and soda water. Stir thoroughly. The word &ldquo;stir&ldquo; means&hellip;.</p>','1','<p>To make smooth</p>','<p>To boil</p>','<p>To cut</p>','<p>To make dry</p>','<p>To move an object in order to mix it</p>','E','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('177','16','23','<p>Read the following questions!</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>You can make instant noodles with the help of a microwave.</li>\r\n<li>Finally, add any items that you want and serve the noodles.</li>\r\n<li>First, fill the bowl with two cups of water and the noodle.</li>\r\n<li>Microwave it for about three to five minutes.</li>\r\n<li>Then, take the noodles out of the microwave and pour the seasonings.</li>\r\n<li>After the microwave beeps, wait for three minutes in the closed microwave.</li>\r\n<li>Next, stir the noodles until the seasonings dissolve.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>The best arrangement of the sentences above is ...</p>','1','<p>1-7-5-6-2-4-3</p>','<p>1-3-4-6-5-7-2</p>','<p>1-2-7-3-6-5-4</p>','<p>1-4-7-5-2-6-3</p>','<p>1-2-3-4-5-6-7</p>','B','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('178','16','24','<p>Read the following questions!</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>You can make instant noodles with the help of a microwave.</li>\r\n<li>Finally, add any items that you want and serve the noodles.</li>\r\n<li>First, fill the bowl with two cups of water and the noodle.</li>\r\n<li>Microwave it for about three to five minutes.</li>\r\n<li>Then, take the noodles out of the microwave and pour the seasonings.</li>\r\n<li>After the microwave beeps, wait for three minutes in the closed microwave.</li>\r\n<li>Next, stir the noodles until the seasonings dissolve.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>How long should you microwave the noodles?</p>','1','<p>1-2 minutes</p>','<p>8 minutes.</p>','<p>7-10 minutes.</p>','<p>15 minutes</p>','<p>3-5 minutes.</p>','E','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('179','16','25','<p>&ldquo;Instruction Burning CD with two CD trays&rdquo;</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Insert the CD, from which you want to burn the file, into the computer&rsquo;s CD tray.</li>\r\n<li>Insert a blank CD you want to copy the files to, into the second CD tray on your computer.</li>\r\n<li>Open &ldquo;Windows Media Player&rdquo; and wait for it to read the CD.</li>\r\n<li>At the top of Windows Media Player, click &ldquo;Burn&rdquo;.</li>\r\n<li>Drag the files you want to burn into the area on the right side called &ldquo;Burn List&rdquo;.</li>\r\n<li>Choose the blank CD that you want to burn your files onto from the top of the &ldquo;Burn List&rdquo; menu.</li>\r\n<li>After you choose all the files you want to burn, click &ldquo;Start Burn&rdquo;. Wait for the computer to finish and then take out both of your CDs.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>What is the topic of the text?</p>','1','<p>How to insert a CD</p>','<p>How to copy files from a CD</p>','<p>How to burn CD with two CD trays</p>','<p>How to operate a computer</p>','<p>How to delete some files</p>','C','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('180','16','26','<p>&ldquo;Instruction Burning CD with two CD trays&rdquo;</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li><strong>Insert</strong> the CD, from which you want to burn the file, into the computer&rsquo;s CD tray.</li>\r\n<li>Insert a blank CD you want to copy the files to, into the second CD tray on your computer.</li>\r\n<li>Open &ldquo;Windows Media Player&rdquo; and wait for it to read the CD.</li>\r\n<li>At the top of Windows Media Player, click &ldquo;Burn&rdquo;.</li>\r\n<li>Drag the files you want to burn into the area on the right side called &ldquo;Burn List&rdquo;.</li>\r\n<li>Choose the blank CD that you want to burn your files onto from the top of the &ldquo;Burn List&rdquo; menu.</li>\r\n<li>After you choose all the files you want to burn, click &ldquo;Start Burn&rdquo;. Wait for the computer to finish and then take out both of your CDs.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>The word<strong> &ldquo;insert&rdquo;</strong> has similar meaning to &hellip;.</p>','1','<p>Put into</p>','<p>Take out</p>','<p>Give</p>','<p>Bring</p>','<p>Execute</p>','A','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('181','16','27','<p>&ldquo;Instruction Burning CD with two CD trays&rdquo;</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Insert the CD, from which you want to burn the file, into the computer&rsquo;s CD tray.</li>\r\n<li>Insert a blank CD you want to copy the files to, into the second CD tray on your computer.</li>\r\n<li>Open &ldquo;Windows Media Player&rdquo; and wait for it to read the CD.</li>\r\n<li>At the top of Windows Media Player, click &ldquo;Burn&rdquo;.</li>\r\n<li>Drag the files you want to burn into the area on the right side called &ldquo;Burn List&rdquo;.</li>\r\n<li>Choose the blank CD that you want to burn your files onto from the top of the &ldquo;Burn List&rdquo; menu.</li>\r\n<li>After you choose all the files you want to burn, click &ldquo;Start Burn&rdquo;. Wait for the computer to finish and then take out both of your CDs.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>What should we do after click &ldquo;burn&rdquo;?</p>','1','<p>Click &ldquo;start burn&rdquo;</p>','<p>Choose the blank CD</p>','<p>Insert the CD</p>','<p>Drag the files from the list of files into the &ldquo;burn list&rdquo; area</p>','<p>Open windows media player and wait for it to read the CD</p>','B','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('182','16','28','<ol>\r\n<li>Turn on the camera: Locate the power button and press it to turn on the camera.</li>\r\n<li>Choose the shooting mode: Most cameras have different shooting modes, such as automatic, manual, aperture priority, and shutter priority. Select the mode that best suits your needs.</li>\r\n<li>Frame your shot: Compose your photo by adjusting the camera\'s angle and position. Use the viewfinder or LCD screen to see the scene.</li>\r\n<li>Focus the camera: Ensure that the subject is in focus by using the autofocus system or manually adjusting the focus.</li>\r\n<li>Adjust the exposure: Control the brightness of the photo by adjusting the aperture and shutter speed. You can also use the ISO setting to control the camera\'s sensitivity to light.</li>\r\n<li>Take the photo: Press the shutter button to take the photo.</li>\r\n<li>Review the photo: View the photo on the LCD screen to see if it is to your liking.</li>\r\n<li>Delete or save the photo: If you are not satisfied with the photo, you can delete it. Otherwise, save it to the camera\'s memory card.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>What are some common shooting modes found on cameras?</p>','1','<p>Automatic, manual, aperture priority, and shutter priority</p>','<p>Zoom, focus, flash, and timer.</p>','<p>Portrait, landscape, sports, and night.</p>','<p>Aperture, shutter speed, and ISO.</p>','<p>All of the above.</p>','A','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('183','16','29','<ol>\r\n<li>Turn on the camera: Locate the power button and press it to turn on the camera.</li>\r\n<li>Choose the shooting mode: Most cameras have different shooting modes, such as automatic, manual, aperture priority, and shutter priority. Select the mode that best suits your needs.</li>\r\n<li>Frame your shot: Compose your photo by adjusting the camera\'s angle and position. Use the viewfinder or LCD screen to see the scene.</li>\r\n<li>Focus the camera: Ensure that the subject is in focus by using the autofocus system or manually adjusting the focus.</li>\r\n<li>Adjust the exposure: Control the brightness of the photo by adjusting the aperture and shutter speed. You can also use the ISO setting to control the camera\'s sensitivity to light.</li>\r\n<li>Take the photo: Press the shutter button to take the photo.</li>\r\n<li>Review the photo: View the photo on the LCD screen to see if it is to your liking.</li>\r\n<li>Delete or save the photo: If you are not satisfied with the photo, you can delete it. Otherwise, save it to the camera\'s memory card.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>After taking a photo, what should you do?</p>','1','<p>Delete it immediately.</p>','<p>Review it on the LCD screen</p>','<p>Adjust the exposure.</p>','<p>Frame the shot.</p>','<p>Delete it.</p>','B','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('184','16','30','<ol>\r\n<li>Turn on the camera: Locate the power button and press it to turn on the camera.</li>\r\n<li>Choose the shooting mode: Most cameras have different shooting modes, such as automatic, manual, aperture priority, and shutter priority. Select the mode that best suits your needs.</li>\r\n<li>Frame your shot: Compose your photo by adjusting the camera\'s angle and position. Use the viewfinder or LCD screen to see the scene.</li>\r\n<li>Focus the camera: Ensure that the subject is in focus by using the autofocus system or manually adjusting the focus.</li>\r\n<li>Adjust the exposure: Control the brightness of the photo by adjusting the aperture and shutter speed. You can also use the ISO setting to control the camera\'s sensitivity to light.</li>\r\n<li>Take the photo: Press the shutter button to take the photo.</li>\r\n<li>Review the photo: View the photo on the LCD screen to see if it is to your liking.</li>\r\n<li>Delete or save the photo: If you are not satisfied with the photo, you can delete it. Otherwise, save it to the camera\'s memory card.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>The goal of the text above is to tell about &hellip;.</p>','1','<p>How to take a well-composed photo of a landscape.</p>','<p>How to become a professional photographer</p>','<p>how to operate a camera</p>','<p>How to make a camera</p>','<p>How to take take a photo</p>','C','','','','','','','');
INSERT INTO `soal` VALUES ('225','16','10','<ol>\r\n<li>Power On: Locate the power button on your computer\'s case or monitor. Press it to turn on the computer.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Using the Mouse:</strong> Left-click to select items, right-click to open a context menu, and drag and drop to move items.</li>\r\n<li>Login: If prompted, enter your username and password to access your user account.</li>\r\n<li>Desktop: The desktop is the main screen where you interact with your computer.</li>\r\n<li>Icons: These are shortcuts to applications, files, and folders. Double-click an icon to open the corresponding item.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; How do you open an application?</p>','1','<p>Press the power button</p>','<p>Right-click on the application\'s icon</p>','<p>Left-click on the application\'s icon</p>','<p>Double-click the application\'s icon</p>','<p>Drag and drop the application\'s icon</p>','D','','','','','','','');
